        "title": "First Light",
        "subtitle": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "poem",
        "id": "poem-0",
        "title": "Inventory",
        "body": "Three cups, one cracked along the rim,\na window with a view of rain,\nthe kettle arguing with itself,\nand nothing here I need explain.",
        "dedication": "",
        "note": "after nobody in particular"
      },
      {
        "kind": "poem",
        "id": "poem-1",
        "title": "Hours",
        "body": "The morning keeps its own accounts.\nThe afternoon forgets to write.\nBy evening every sum is wrong\nand somehow settles up by night.",
        "dedication": "",
        "note": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "poem",
        "id": "poem-2",
        "title": "Small Weather",
        "body": "A draught came in beneath the door\nand made the candle lean and stay.\nI let it lean. I let the room\nbe smaller than it was by day.",
        "dedication": "",
        "note": ""
      }
